After a nice streak of five ascension the Random Torture Generator
presented me an archeologist that I had the task to lead through the
dungeons; a difficult task because (at NAO) I never succeeded with
that class.

The game began promising with an early coaligned altar and an early
ring that turned out to be regeneration. But food and armor was as
usual my problem with that class. My pet died early and I was on my
own. Because of the food problems I abstained from taming some cats,
dogs, and horses that attacked me; so I just pacified them by food
that they don't like to eat.

Level after level I had problems to survive, hordes of insects and
other critters made me nearly die many times, and I have to retreat
and flee to other levels... where the same happened. Nowhere to go!
So I chose the mines. Since the level was dark and I didn't have any
armor that's worth to mention (just 3 points of protection) I wanted
to dive down to minetown with my pickaxe to get some basic armor; a
difficult task to dig while the critters try to kill you. The second
mine level was lit but unfortunately three soldier ants attacked me.
